questions.question_text:
The diagram shows the graph of $y = f(x)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1.9, xmax=3.9, ymin=-7.8, ymax=3.8, xtick={-1,1,2,3}, ytick={-6,-4,-2,2}, samples=100, clip=false, width=9cm, height=8cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-1.19:3.35] {x*x*x - 3*x*x - 1};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
For which values of $x$ is $f''(x) > 0$?

questions.solution_text:
$y' = 6x^2 + 6x - 12$
$= 6(x + 2)(x - 1)$
$x = -2$ or $x = 1$
$y(-2) = -16 + 12 + 24 + 4 = 24$
$y(1) = 2 + 3 - 12 + 4 = -3$
$y'' = 12x + 6$
$y''(-2) = -18 < 0$, so $(-2, 24)$ is a maximum.
$y''(1) = 18 > 0$, so $(1, -3)$ is a minimum.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-4.2, xmax=3.4, ymin=-9.5, ymax=31, xtick={-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3}, ytick={-5,5,10,15,20,25,30}, samples=100, clip=false, width=9cm, height=9cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-3.63:2.63] {2*x*x*x + 3*x*x - 12*x + 4};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:-2,24) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:1,-3) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:-0.5,10.5) {};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$y' = 12x^3 - 24x^2$
$= 12x^2(x - 2)$
$x = 0$ or $x = 2$
$y' = 12x^2(x - 2)$ is negative on both sides of $x = 0$, so $(0, 6)$ is a horizontal point of inflection.
$y'' = 36x^2 - 48x$
$y''(2) = 144 - 96 = 48 > 0$, so $(2, -10)$ is a minimum.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1.4, xmax=3.4, ymin=-16, ymax=16, xtick={-1,1,2,3}, ytick={-15,-10,-5,5,10,15}, samples=120, clip=false, width=8cm, height=8cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-0.9:2.78] {3*x*x*x*x - 8*x*x*x + 6};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:0,6) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:2,-10) {};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The function is undefined when the denominator is zero.
$x + 3 = 0$
$x = -3$
$\dfrac{2x - 1}{x + 3} = 2 - \dfrac{7}{x + 3}$
As $x \to -3^{-}$, $y \to \infty$; as $x \to -3^{+}$, $y \to -\infty$, so $x = -3$ is a vertical asymptote.
As $x \to \pm\infty$ the fraction tends to $0$, so $y = 2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-10, xmax=5, ymin=-5.8, ymax=9.8, xtick={-9,-6,-3,3}, ytick={-4,-2,2,4,6,8}, samples=150, clip=false, width=10cm, height=8cm]
\addplot[dashed] coordinates {(-3,-5.8) (-3,9.8)};
\addplot[dashed] coordinates {(-10,2) (5,2)};
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-9.5:-4.05] {(2*x - 1)/(x + 3)};
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-1.98:4.8] {(2*x - 1)/(x + 3)};
\node[above left, font=\small] at (axis cs:-3.1,8.4) {$x = -3$};
\node[above, font=\small] at (axis cs:2.5,2.1) {$y = 2$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$(1 - x)e^{-x} = 0$
Since $e^{-x} > 0$ for all $x$, $x = 1$ and $f(1) = e^{-1}$.
$f''(1) = (1 - 2)e^{-1} = -e^{-1} < 0$, so $(1, e^{-1})$ is a maximum.
$(x - 2)e^{-x} = 0$
$x = 2$ and $f(2) = 2e^{-2}$
$f''$ changes from negative to positive at $x = 2$, so $(2, 2e^{-2})$ is a point of inflection.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-1.2, xmax=6.6, ymin=-1.3, ymax=0.8, xtick={-1,1,2,3,4,5,6}, ytick={-1,-0.5,0.5}, samples=150, clip=false, width=10cm, height=7cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-0.61:6] {x*exp(-x)};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:1,0.3679) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:2,0.2707) {};
\node[above, font=\small] at (axis cs:1,0.42) {$(1,e^{-1})$};
\node[above right, font=\small] at (axis cs:2.15,0.29) {$(2,2e^{-2})$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

questions.question_text:
The diagram shows the graph of $y = f(x)$ with four points marked.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.7, xmax=3.4, ymin=-3.6, ymax=8.6, xtick={1,2,3}, ytick={2,4,6,8}, samples=120, clip=false, width=9cm, height=8cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-0.2:2.9] {2*x*x*x - 9*x*x + 12*x};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:0.4,3.488) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:1.3,4.784) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:1.75,4.15625) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:2.6,5.512) {};
\node[above left] at (axis cs:0.4,3.488) {$A$};
\node[above] at (axis cs:1.3,4.9) {$B$};
\node[below] at (axis cs:1.75,4.05) {$C$};
\node[right] at (axis cs:2.65,5.512) {$D$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
At which point is $f'(x) < 0$ and $f''(x) > 0$?

questions.solution_text:
$y' = 3x^2 + 2bx + c$
At the stationary point $x = -1$:
$3 - 2b + c = 0$
At the stationary point $x = 3$:
$27 + 6b + c = 0$
Subtracting the first equation from the second gives $24 + 8b = 0$, so $b = -3$.
Substituting into $27 + 6b + c = 0$:
$27 - 18 + c = 0$
$c = -9$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-3.9, xmax=5.9, ymin=-29, ymax=21, xtick={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5}, ytick={-20,-10,10,20}, samples=100, clip=false, width=10cm, height=9cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-3.14:5.14] {x*x*x - 3*x*x - 9*x + 7};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:-1,12) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:3,-20) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:1,-4) {};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$y' = -2\sin x + 1$
$-2\sin x + 1 = 0$
$\sin x = \dfrac{1}{2}$
$x = \dfrac{\pi}{6}$ or $x = \dfrac{5\pi}{6}$
$y'' = -2\cos x$
$y''\left(\dfrac{\pi}{6}\right) = -\sqrt{3} < 0$, so $x = \dfrac{\pi}{6}$ gives a maximum.
$y''\left(\dfrac{5\pi}{6}\right) = \sqrt{3} > 0$, so $x = \dfrac{5\pi}{6}$ gives a minimum.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.8, xmax=7.3, ymin=-1, ymax=9.6, xtick={1.5708,3.1416,4.7124,6.2832}, xticklabels={$\frac{\pi}{2}$,$\pi$,$\frac{3\pi}{2}$,$2\pi$}, ytick={2,4,6,8}, samples=150, clip=false, width=10cm, height=8cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, domain=0:6.2832] {2*cos(deg(x)) + x};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:0.5236,2.2556) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:2.618,0.8859) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:0,2) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:6.2832,8.2832) {};
\node[above right, font=\small] at (axis cs:0.6,2.3) {$x=\frac{\pi}{6}$};
\node[below, font=\small] at (axis cs:2.618,0.8) {$x=\frac{5\pi}{6}$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$y' = \ln x + x \times \dfrac{1}{x}$
$= \ln x + 1$
$\ln x + 1 = 0$
$\ln x = -1$
$x = e^{-1}$
$y = e^{-1} \times \ln\left(e^{-1}\right) = -e^{-1}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-0.5, xmax=2.7, ymin=-1, ymax=2.2, xtick={1,2}, ytick={-0.5,0.5,1,1.5,2}, samples=200, clip=false, width=9cm, height=8cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, ->, domain=0.015:2.2] {x*ln(x)};
\node[circle, draw, fill=white, inner sep=1.3pt] at (axis cs:0,0) {};
\node[circle, fill, inner sep=1.5pt] at (axis cs:0.3679,-0.3679) {};
\node[below right, font=\small] at (axis cs:0.42,-0.4) {$\left(e^{-1},-e^{-1}\right)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
